<div class="side-by-side">
  <p class="big">Invitational: risk, reward and a blind offer</p>
  <p>
    Ten teams of three, each pairing a COD: Mobile creator with a mobile FPS
    creator and a non-endemic PC creator, competed for a $50K prize pool over
    three loot-race rounds. After each round, teams secretly bid DMZ Cash for a
    share of the pool, and only the top offers were paid out. Bidding meant
    risk. Not bidding meant giving up cash for a long-term edge. The offers were
    blind, so no team could copy another. In one round, a bid just $1 higher
    than a rival’s was worth an extra $1,000.
  </p>
</div>

